xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;has exactly two solutions", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca61"}, {"id": "52326a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#34;</mo></msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca62"}, {"id": "762074", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;has a root in the interval&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca63"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca64", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfb0a"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b455b"], "concepts": ["60e2fafa66f9ce3f243b4944"], "question": {"text": "The position of a moving car at time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi></math>&nbsp;are real numbers greater than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>.&nbsp;Then the average speed of the car over the time interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is attained at the point:"}, "options": [{"id": "094ecf", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca65"}, {"id": "96aec1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca66"}, {"id": "195777", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca67"}, {"id": "d99cda", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca68"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca69", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfb0a"], "topics": ["60ced3320e34b73944ddfad9"], "concepts": ["60e2faab66f9ce3f243b44f0"], "question": {"text": "<p>A wire of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is to be cut into two pieces. One of the pieces is to be made into a square and the other into a regular hexagon. Then the length of the side (in meters) of the hexagon, so that the combined area of the square and the hexagon is minimum, is</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "12dbc1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca6a"}, {"id": "83c01c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca6b"}, {"id": "787706", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca6c"}, {"id": "3f4329", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca6d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca6e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfb0a"], "topics": ["60ced5dc19d2aa2b78a3a762"], "concepts": ["61923f2fd42d105914c0f42f"], "question": {"text": "<p>The set of all&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math>&nbsp;for which the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>|</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>|</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> has exactly one real root, is</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "a931a2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca6f"}, {"id": "b64c8f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca70"}, {"id": "c2efde", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca71"}, {"id": "ae3aab", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca72"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca73", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfb0a"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b455b"], "concepts": ["60e2fafa66f9ce3f243b4944"], "question": {"text": "A spherical iron ball of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math> is coated with a layer of ice of uniform thickness that melts at a rate of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;When the thickness of the ice is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then the rate at which the thickness <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo></math>in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;of the ice decreases, is :"}, "options": [{"id": "5854ec", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>9</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca74"}, {"id": "6ca714", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>36</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca75"}, {"id": "49933b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>18</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca76"}, {"id": "db74ba", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca77"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca78", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfb0a"], "topics": ["60ced3320e34b73944ddfad9"], "concepts": ["6162fc6e6ed13040ec85a6a4"], "question": {"text": "For the function\n$f(x)=\\sin x+3 x-\\frac{2}{\\pi}\\left(x^2+x\\right), \\text { where } x \\in\\left[0, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right],$\nconsider the following two statements :\n(I) $\\mathrm{f}$ is increasing in $\\left(0, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$.\n(II) $f^{\\prime}$ is decreasing in $\\left(0, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$.<br />Between the above two statements,"}, "options": [{"id": "9af881", "text": "only (II) is true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca79"}, {"id": "67a3f2", "text": "only (I) is true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca7a"}, {"id": "572e5f", "text": "neither (I) nor (II) is true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca7b"}, {"id": "8dd14e", "text": "both (I) and (II) are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca7c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca7d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfb0a"], "topics": ["60ced5dc19d2aa2b78a3a762"], "concepts": ["6162fc6d6ed13040ec85a59d"], "question": {"text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>cos</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>cot</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is the range of the function, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to"}, "options": [{"id": "9e328c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca7e"}, {"id": "9d4782", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#960;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca7f"}, {"id": "a9ef38", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#960;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca80"}, {"id": "87c297", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#960;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca81"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca82", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfb0a"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b455b"], "concepts": ["60e2fafa66f9ce3f243b4944"], "question": {"text": "A spherical iron ball of <math><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> radius is coated with a layer of ice of uniform thickness that melts at a rate of <math><mn>50</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></mrow></math> . When the thickness of ice is <math><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> , then the rate (in <math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></mrow></math> .) at which of the thickness of ice decreases, is:"}, "options": [{"id": "bbb300", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca83"}, {"id": "6e0456", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>54</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca84"}, {"id": "bca667", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>36</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca85"}, {"id": "3fa03e", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>18</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca86"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f682ee0e063d927ca87", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfb0a"], "topics": ["60ced3320e34b73944ddfad9"], "concepts": ["60e567c4499d1e49588f995e"], "question": {"text": "<p>A box open from top is made from a rectangular sheet of dimension <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>b</mi></math> by cutting squares each of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> from each of the four corners and folding up the flaps. If the volume of the box is maximum, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is equal to:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "e455ff", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></